====================================================================
(A) every tournament on n<=6 vertices: Aut is ODD-order and <= A_n
====================================================================
  n | #tournaments | all |Aut| odd? | all Aut <= A_n (even perms)? | max|Aut|
  1 |           1 |          True |                         True | 1
  2 |           2 |          True |                         True | 1
  3 |           8 |          True |                         True | 3
  4 |          64 |          True |                         True | 3
  5 |        1024 |          True |                         True | 5
  6 |       32768 |          True |                         True | 9
  -> CONFIRMED: no tournament has an order-2 automorphism; |Aut| always odd;
     every automorphism is an EVEN permutation (Aut(T) <= A_n).

====================================================================
(B) Paley_7 tournament: Aut = Z/7 |x Z/3, order 21 (the forbidden value)
====================================================================
  connection set (QR mod 7) = [1, 2, 4] = <2> = cube roots of unity (S640)
  |Aut(Paley_7)| = 21   (= 21 = 3*7 = forbidden H-value? True)
  element orders in Aut = [1, 3, 7]  (all ODD; contains order-3 = the cube root)
  derived series orders: [21, 7, 1, 1]  (reaches 1 => SOLVABLE, NOT perfect)
  structure: Z/7 (additive, normal) |x Z/3 (the doubling <2>=cube root); 
  derived length 2: peel Z/3 (cube root, top) then Z/7 (bottom) -- a SOLVABLE
  shell-tower. The cube root is a SOLVABLE LAYER here, not a no-formula source.

====================================================================
(C) the cyclotomic / LRC side is abelian => solvable (derived length <=1)
====================================================================
  (Z/7)* has order 6; abelian => solvable (derived length 1). <2>-doubling orbit of 1: [1, 2, 4] (the LRC shell)
  (Z/14)* has order 6; abelian => solvable (derived length 1). <2>-doubling orbit of 1: [1, 2, 4, 8] (the LRC shell)
  (Z/15)* has order 8; abelian => solvable (derived length 1). <2>-doubling orbit of 1: [1, 2, 4, 8] (the LRC shell)
  (Z/22)* has order 10; abelian => solvable (derived length 1). <2>-doubling orbit of 1: [1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 10, 20, 18, 14, 6, 12] (the LRC shell)
  the LRC cyclotomic Galois group (Z/n)* is ABELIAN: solvable trivially.
  the shell-tower (doubling orbits) is a subgroup chain inside an abelian group.

====================================================================
(D) the bracket: two great solvability theorems, two sides of FTA duality
====================================================================
  ROOTS  (S_n, generic Galois): Abel-Ruffini -> UNSOLVABLE for n>=5 (needs swaps).
  PERSPECTIVES (Aut(T)): no involution -> ODD order -> Feit-Thompson -> SOLVABLE,
       and Aut(T) <= A_n. The swap sigma is the CONVERSE (anti-automorphism, S638),
       deliberately OUTSIDE Aut. So perspectives never reach a perfect group: the
       'no formula' wall (A_5) is the ONE wall the tournament/LRC arc does NOT cross.
